# SiliconBoard LLM keys. Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit .env.
#
# Providers are tried in order: the first with a key and a working model wins,
# and the rest are fallbacks. All of them are optional on their own.
#
# Gemini. Rate limits are per Google Cloud project, not per key, so four keys
# only multiply your quota if they come from four separate projects. The model
# ids below are the ones that exist today; 2.5-pro and 2.5-flash are shut down.
# GEMINI_API_KEY_1=
# GEMINI_API_KEY_2=
# GEMINI_API_KEY_3=
# GEMINI_API_KEY_4=

# Groq. OpenAI-compatible, open models, free tier. This is what the project has
# actually been running on, and it is the cheapest reliable option.
# GROQ_API_KEY_1=
# GROQ_API_KEY_2=
# GROQ_API_KEY_3=
# GROQ_API_KEY_4=

# OpenAI. Sits between gemini and groq in the chains, so it only gets called when
# both of those are unavailable. Cost per token is far higher than either, which is
# the point of it being third and not first. Any number of keys works; they rotate.
# OPENAI_API_KEY_1=
# OPENAI_API_KEY_2=
# OPENAI_API_KEY_3=

# Amazon Bedrock. A Bedrock API key is a single bearer token, not an AWS access
# key pair. If you use SigV4 IAM credentials instead, give the id and secret the
# same slot numbers and leave BEDROCK_API_KEY_* empty.
BEDROCK_API_KEY_1=
BEDROCK_API_KEY_2=
BEDROCK_API_KEY_3=
AWS_BEDROCK_REGION=ap-south-1

# Nvidia build endpoint. Every model in the old chain has since been retired
# (410 Gone), so this only works if you pick a current one explicitly.
# NVIDIA_API_KEY=

# Cost. A full run is cheap and a replay is free. The live counter run measured
# (tokens in/out): spec 340/823, RTL 719/568, testbench 1190/6383, timing 756/1261,
# report 1554/1655 - about 4.6k in and 10.7k out. Output is billed with thinking
# included (llm._billed_output adds thoughtsTokenCount, which runs ~15x the visible
# answer on a thinking model), so the thinking tokens are the bulk of the cost.
# Only RTL and testbench use the HEAVY chain; spec, timing and report take LIGHT.
# Even at a pro-tier rate of ~$10 per million output tokens that is on the order of
# ten cents per run, so a ~$90 budget covers hundreds of uncached runs. A run
# replayed from board.json makes zero llm calls, and a cached run is also free.